mode: "100644"
text: "# The Remix — executing a trend-jack\n\nA trend has cleared all three gates. Now the job is to ride it **fast** while adding your **own\nangle** — because a logo-slapped copy of a viral video earns nothing, but the trend's structure +\nyour perspective can.\n\n## Add an angle, don't just copy\n\nThe difference between a trend-jack that works and one that flops:\n\n- **Copy** — recreate the viral video with your product in it. Generic, forgettable, slightly\n  embarrassing.\n- **Remix** — take the trend's **structure/sound/format** and fill it with **your niche's specific\n  truth**. The familiarity of the trend + the freshness of your angle is what earns the share.\n\nAsk: *what does this trend look like through our world?* A trending \"expectation vs reality\" format\nbecomes *your customers'* expectation vs reality. A trending sound scores *your* niche's running\njoke. The trend is the vehicle; your perspective is the payload.\n\n## Keep the brand voice\n\nA trend-jack still sounds like you. Don't abandon `voice.md` to chase trend-speak — forced slang and\nout-of-character energy read as a brand trying too hard. The best version feels like *your brand\nnoticed the trend and had something to say*, not like you hired a teenager for one post. Translate\nthe trend into your voice, don't translate your voice into the trend.\n\n## Add value or wit, not just presence\n\nEarn the spot in the feed: be **funny**, **useful**, **relatable**, or **surprising** with your\nangle. Mere participation (\"we're doing the trend too!\") isn't enough. The trend gets you the\nattention; the angle decides whether it converts to a follow/share or a scroll.\n\n## Speed without sloppiness\n\nTrends decay, so move fast — but \"fast\" means **decisive**, not careless. The gates are non-negotiable\neven under time pressure (a fast safety mistake is the expensive kind). Keep production light and\nnative (especially on TikTok — handheld beats polished); ship while the window's open. Hand execution\nto the right content skill so it's still well-made:\n\n- short video → `tiktok-script` / `reels-script`\n- caption/text → `caption-writer`\n- carousel → `carousel-writer`\n- then schedule/publish → `scheduling-and-queue`.\n\n## The fast lane (for brands/teams)\n\nTrend-jacking dies in approval chains — by the time legal signs off, the trend is dead. So set up a\n**fast lane in advance**:\n\n- Pre-agree **guardrails** (the SAFETY hard-no list, brand voice, what's off-limits) so trends that\n  fit can ship within hours without a committee.\n- Name **who can approve** a trend-jack quickly.\n- Anything that touches the caution/no zones still escalates — the fast lane is for clearly-safe\n  trends only.\n\n## Don't over-chase — reactive complements evergreen\n\nTrend-jacking is the **reactive** slot, not the whole strategy. A brand that *only* chases trends has\nno identity, exhausts its team, and rides other people's moments forever. Keep it as a portion of the\nmix (the reactive slots in `content-calendar`), on top of evergreen pillar content that builds who\nyou actually are. Ride trends to get discovered; post your own content to be remembered.\n\n## Measure honestly\n\nDon't claim a trend-jack worked without numbers. Judge it by whether it **fit, was safe, and\nlanded** (native platform insights the user pulls, or qualitative read), not by metrics this skill\ncan't provide. One trend-jack flopping isn't failure; forcing the next one would be.\n"
